<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:53Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India: Cockroach Janta Party leaders allege mass detentions ahead of Delhi protest, decry 'emergency'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e86fc1bbcdcb0637fec2b8f1301ac1a5dd6d830fe90e85f5354dd075ac09dcb</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:36Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T06:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-cockroach-janta-party-leaders-allege-mass-detentions-ahead-of-delhi-protest-decry-emergency/live-79606961--cb6e3c288ef9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-cockroach-janta-party-leaders-allege-mass-detentions-ahead-of-delhi-protest-decry-emergency/live-79606961?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Cockroach Janta Party claims authorities are carrying out mass arrests ahead of its planned protest on October 10. Founder 'Cockroach' Abhijeet Dipke has accused the Modi government of "intimidation." DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Two German officials shot dead during routine gun inspection in Bavaria; suspect arrested after overnight standoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b82d41b40e6858da4945d3f38270acf5016233a41a039bfdf2f856e392817550</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T05:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/two-german-officials-shot-dead-during-routine-gun-inspection-in-bavaria-suspect-arrested-after-overn/live-79607225--1b63007f86d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/two-german-officials-shot-dead-during-routine-gun-inspection-in-bavaria-suspect-arrested-after-overnight-standoff/live-79607225?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A routine inspection of legally owned firearms turned deadly in Bavaria. Police spent hours negotiating with an armed suspect before storming his home. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Europe, US to meet in Miami for talks on ending war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f4d860125e178defd5a409bf2ac3be01badbc6f90d81dd30b8fe49c8aec6b4e5</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T03:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-europe-us-to-meet-in-miami-for-talks-on-ending-war/a-79606735--3bdeeca19288.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-europe-us-to-meet-in-miami-for-talks-on-ending-war/a-79606735?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Officials from Ukraine, Europe and the US are meeting in Miami to discuss ways to break the deadlock in the war. The meeting comes as Russian strikes on Ukraine killed more than 70 people this week.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Man injured after New York shooting involving ICE</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f977ab0a2fdfa923c0fb75ea8d8212a4c5b1c6df72b2b71bf30ec984ab16839</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T00:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/man-injured-after-new-york-shooting-involving-ice/a-79606159--3bab6661b521.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/man-injured-after-new-york-shooting-involving-ice/a-79606159?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New York City Mayor Zohran Mamdani has condemned the incident and urged Donald Trump to end ICE actions in the city. The man was being treated at a nearby hospital, New York police said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US to livestream Fort Hood shooter's execution: Pentagon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5ffc3340a4cfe9ea00045d3bdb0da0d3d3951a4e6d6d11035debebf6846c8eb</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T23:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-to-livestream-fort-hood-shooter-s-execution-pentagon/a-79606395--883a2bcd9edf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-to-livestream-fort-hood-shooter-s-execution-pentagon/a-79606395?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US Pentagon chief Pete Hegseth had said that Nidal Hasan would be executed by firing squad and that it would be done "in public." Hasan's execution will be the first by the US military since 1961.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ex-German Chancellor Schröder attends Putin's birthday bash</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82a0d14e69ba0be0db0319906269e0bcc44cca49f4aa2c0f9c1709efaadae91c</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:51Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T22:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ex-german-chancellor-schr_der-attends-putin-s-birthday-bash/a-79606017--884ded06e661.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ex-german-chancellor-schröder-attends-putin-s-birthday-bash/a-79606017?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Chancellor Gerhard Schröder still maintains a friendship with Russian leader Vladimir Putin. Tensions are high between Germany and Russia as the invasion of Ukraine continues.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Two Latvian men arrested for breaking into RAF base</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cb2729297bbd7a1be902539a8bc3edd2bec5656a64e5cba9434cf45c9e434d0</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T22:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-two-latvian-men-arrested-for-breaking-into-raf-base/a-79606026--0c8c81f09e63.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-two-latvian-men-arrested-for-breaking-into-raf-base/a-79606026?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The men were arrested for breaching a perimeter fence at a UK air base that houses US and NATO intelligence operations. The incident comes after an alleged terror plot at another air base in England was foiled recently.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Afghan women facing arrest for dress code violations: UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1e20150521bd1915ecba4c3ca30c983fb35fb417eeb836551ca117227552608</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-facing-arrest-for-dress-code-violations-un/a-79605758--a597af505f96.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghan-women-facing-arrest-for-dress-code-violations-un/a-79605758?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In recent months, the Taliban authorities in Afghanistan have arrested or detained dozens of women for alleged violations of dress codes and for appearing in public without a male guardian.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US suspends Microsoft, Adobe from filing for green cards</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4d42162addbc3687d4b935cf239dc573c3163038daf2ee3ae1bd5fbb3340d4e5</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T20:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-suspends-microsoft-adobe-from-filing-for-green-cards/a-79605053--bd3960bfb6cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-suspends-microsoft-adobe-from-filing-for-green-cards/a-79605053?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration cut off tech firms, including Microsoft and Adobe, from filing for green cards for their foreign workers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Africa: Anti-migrant protests turn violent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbf5cd4870a5b329a85636b94eec9396848b0443d54d4f3992db07db7512eee4</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T18:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-africa-anti-migrant-protests-turn-violent/a-79605037--9e8292035a94.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-africa-anti-migrant-protests-turn-violent/a-79605037?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A court order requiring the government to resume processing asylum applications reignited violent protests against immigration in South Africa.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US will not resume strikes on Iran before midterms — Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e6d92c861e51e55c0870e5be0f7968add7e23d5f11acacc67f39da033e9e0ced</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T18:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-will-not-resume-strikes-on-iran-before-midterms-trump/a-79603731--e9422c274a9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-will-not-resume-strikes-on-iran-before-midterms-trump/a-79603731?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump said the US will not resume strikes on Iran before the midterm elections on November 3. High gas and grocery prices are top concerns for voters.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Police clash with protesters at Paris student rally</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9a1c8d3a6758caaa0ba69f3f5b4d2d8bce6e37b8665b08328268d7df5e76b05</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T17:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-police-clash-with-protesters-at-paris-student-rally/a-79603684--e3a1d23b72a1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-police-clash-with-protesters-at-paris-student-rally/a-79603684?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police fired tear gas at protesters in Paris again as students continue to voice grievances about school conditions across France. The education minister has said 3,000 substitute teachers will reach schools soon.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US prosecutors add new torture charge against Maduro</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6e176047fbbf923dc42b4f5e52bb5154cfebe3494949670cdc472440e5a39e9</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-prosecutors-add-new-torture-charge-against-maduro/a-79588019--2a2967987def.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-prosecutors-add-new-torture-charge-against-maduro/a-79588019?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US prosecutors have added a new charge to their case against deposed Venezuelan leader Nicolas Maduro and his wife, Cilia Flores, accusing the couple of conspiring to commit torture.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU pulls sponsorship from Disinfo2026 event in Lithuania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e697a158c4d203012d5b49fcd51feb7f6e30931c926c2b8fa376633c01c63676</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615--b060dac4b016.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-pulls-sponsorship-from-disinfo2026-event-in-lithuania/a-79599615?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU's diplomatic service, Canada and host nation Lithuania all pulled support from a disinformation event in Vilnius. Amid reports of US pressure, the EU said it was "uncomfortable with the framing" of some panels.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How the Houthi-Saudi conflict is affecting countries on Africa's Red Sea coast — and beyond</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:34b3e8a704929e959738a946c436eab68453c09f57ea27ed50825b2fe9be716f</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T16:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthi-saudi-conflict-is-affecting-countries-on-africa-s-red-sea-coast-and-beyond/a-79588992--cc6ed789d367.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-the-houthi-saudi-conflict-is-affecting-countries-on-africa-s-red-sea-coast-and-beyond/a-79588992?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Bab el-Mandeb Strait, which Yemeni government forces are trying to take back from the Houthis, is located not far from Djibouti and other African states.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Rodrigo Duterte ruled fit to stand trial by ICC judges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6177bfb6a13e67f433af14c4757196e865192678a499c5332af4fff2af8c45b</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rodrigo-duterte-ruled-fit-to-stand-trial-by-icc-judges/a-79599372--793387d40a2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rodrigo-duterte-ruled-fit-to-stand-trial-by-icc-judges/a-79599372?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Judges at the International Criminal Court said Rodrigo Duterte was fit to understand the charges at his trial, which is set to begin in November. His legal team argued that he suffers from cognitive deficiencies.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Nobel Prize winner Anne Carson: Where to start reading</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1114ea736222fefc614ace5932daccc4f8d6af58490bff31a3bb94e19270774a</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/2026-nobel-prize-winner-anne-carson-where-to-start-reading/a-79598953--08cd2959f273.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/2026-nobel-prize-winner-anne-carson-where-to-start-reading/a-79598953?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The works of this year's Nobel Literature Prize-winning poet and essayist Anne Carson can feel slightly daunting. Here are some keys to understanding her universe.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>EU envoy in Beijing for talks to calm trade tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6567d20dc0fc99f306f15d72014a465843bfac17b0e9bf4e6e0f618a56b411e2</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-envoy-in-beijing-for-talks-to-calm-trade-tensions/a-79598713--6570dc66b587.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-envoy-in-beijing-for-talks-to-calm-trade-tensions/a-79598713?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU trade envoy said he hoped to make progress in tackling the bloc's "unsustainable" trade imbalance with China. Beijing called for trade disputes to be resolved through equal dialogue.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b714c532028bce05383771a490e359fc022999569cd8f8b90b8400e042e397eb</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>World Cup 2034: Does Saudi Arabia shelving Neom Stadium spell trouble?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d92f0b8d108c2a57c20d21f01300b1a8882b031fb8deed03287d55c8da5e04d2</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948--b8b608a266b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/world-cup-2034-does-saudi-arabia-shelving-neom-stadium-spell-trouble/a-79592948?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since winning the right to hold the 2034 World Cup unopposed, Saudi Arabia has been pulling away from sport. With reports that its most ambitious stadium project will be abandoned, what does this mean for the World Cup?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Early-onset cancer rising worldwide: Causes, risk, prevention</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d5aeb897cfb31d208f5f669077c6b0009726679df336e765d372c749392496f</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:21:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T13:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097--5416293e8076.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/early-onset-cancer-rising-worldwide-causes-risk-prevention/a-79597097?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Across Latin America, early-onset cancer rates have risen, with Chile and Brazil seeing the fastest growth, especially of bowel, breast and cervical cancers. But it is a worldwide trend.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry></feed>
